Citation:	Fabbri, Bryan (2025): Basic measurements of radiation at station Granite Island (2025-06) [dataset]. NASA Langley Research Center, Hampton, PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.984774, 
	In: Denn, Fred M; Fabbri, Bryan (2024): Basic measurements of radiation at station Granite Island (2019-01 et seq) [dataset publication series]. NASA Langley Research Center, Hampton, PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.971609
Other version:	Fabbri, Bryan (2025): BSRN Station-to-archive file for station Granite Island (2025-06) [dataset]. ftp://ftp.bsrn.awi.de/gim/gim0625.dat.gz
Project(s):	Baseline Surface Radiation Network (BSRN) (URI: https://bsrn.awi.de/)
Coverage:	LATITUDE: 46.721000 * LONGITUDE: -87.411000
	DATE/TIME START: 2025-06-01T00:00:00 * DATE/TIME END: 2025-06-30T23:59:00
	MINIMUM HEIGHT above ground: 2 m * MAXIMUM HEIGHT above ground: 2 m
Event(s):	GIM (Granite Island) (URI: https://science.larc.nasa.gov/CRAVE/) * LATITUDE: 46.721000 * LONGITUDE: -87.411000 * DATE/TIME: 2018-07-01T00:00:00 * ELEVATION: 195.0 m * LOCATION: Lake Superior, Michigan, United States * METHOD/DEVICE: Monitoring station (MONS) * COMMENT: BSRN Station No. 78; Surface type: water, lake; Topography type: flat, rural; Horizon: doi:10.1594/PANGAEA.931000; Station scientist: Bryan Fabbri (bryan.e.fabbri@nasa.gov), Fred Denn (frederick.m.denn@nasa.gov)
Comment:	- Smoke from Canadian wildfires were prevalent over Granite Island this month
	- DIR data looked anomalous on June 9, presumably due to moisture on the optical window due to high RH, this data was removed from ~20.3 - 21.3 GMT. 
	- SWD data removed for several hours on June 12, 16 and a few hours on June 18 due to large residuals. SWD appeared to have larger than expected values. 
	- DIF, DIR and SWD were removed for several hours on June 15 due to very large (over 100 W/m²), that could not be easily explained so they were removed.
